Z||000000||artherd||10-26-2001||01:21 AM||||Hrm, where do I get a set in a hurry?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Car is off the road untill I replace these, must find! (going to call around tommorow, but if a list member has a set that they'd Fexex me, or just a 'go here, they stock them" I'd love you forever!)<P>PS: are there more than one kind of these LOWER 88 year ball joints?<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000001||Phantom Rage||10-26-2001||02:46 AM||||When I had to replace mine, I checked most of my local part stores with no luck.  The only place I could find them was at the Fiero Store.  I can’t remember exactly how much they cost or what brand they are, but I do recall that they were kind of expensive.  As far as time goes, I think it only took a few days for delivery.  Anyway this was a while ago, so things may have changed.  Hopefully there is another supplier who might carry them.  Come to think about it, I do remember someone telling me that GM Parts Direct carried them as well.||||reg||7
Z||000002||mrfiero||10-26-2001||03:10 AM||||I believe TRW and/or McQuay-Norris also makes '88 lower balljoints.<P>I can't remember where I bought my Moog ball joints from, but I thought it was from a local parts store.  I'll check around in the morning and will see if I can get some for you.<P>I believe I paid around $50 apiece for them, but don't quote me on that.<P> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||FastFieros||10-26-2001||09:04 AM||||If you can find them for $50 a piece you better buy them all. I just purchased 4 on special order from NAPA and they hit me for $92 a piece. <P>The uppers are $75 a piece also, so if you can find these please share the info.<P>I have used only 2 this last weekend so if you want to spring for the $200 for the other pair includes Postal EXPRESS mail service to your door, I will sell them to you. I can do pics or parts numbers tonight if you want to try to chase down some in CA.<P>Loyde <A HREF="http://www.fastfieros.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fastfieros.com</A> ||||reg||14
Z||000004||Nashco||10-26-2001||09:06 AM||||If you check out the fiero section at <A HREF="http://www.suspension.com" TARGET=_blank>suspension.com</A> they have McQuay-Norris lowers for the 88 for 49 bucks each.  When I spoke to the salesperson and bought mine, he told me these are made by Moog, and there aren't many left.  I don't know what to take from all of this, but that's what I was told.  They had GREAT customer service, and have very quick shipping.  I highly recommend them; I didn't have any qualms with their service and they had good prices.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000005||Wannabe||10-26-2001||09:08 AM||||I had no problem with the lowers. It's the uppers that are really tough to find.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Nashco||10-26-2001||09:12 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FastFieros:<BR><B>If you can find them for $50 a piece you better buy them all. I just purchased 4 on special order from NAPA and they hit me for $92 a piece. <P>The uppers are $75 a piece also, so if you can find these please share the info.<P>I have used only 2 this last weekend so if you want to spring for the $200 for the other pair includes Postal EXPRESS mail service to your door, I will sell them to you. I can do pics or parts numbers tonight if you want to try to chase down some in CA.<P>Loyde <A HREF="http://www.fastfieros.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fastfieros.com</A> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I got the uppers at <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com" TARGET=_blank>The Fiero Store</A> for 60 bucks a piece plus shipping.  They also have great customer service and fast shipping.  Just goes to show, it pays to look around a little <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  These uppers, and the lowers I mentioned above were the best prices I found from a reputable place.  If anybody knows better, please let us 88 owners know!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000007||FastFieros||10-26-2001||09:44 AM||||Yup, the upper at $75 did include the shipping also, so this is not too bad. The lower however was on there shelf and it is package in a NAPA box with a part part that was 160-???? I cant remember the rest. I looked on the bottom but MOOG was not stamped on it either. I had a 88 GT I sold to a guy and it had a replacement lower already on it that did have MOOG stamped on it. The part number on it was 78??, darn I didnt write that one down. <P>Best I can tell you from here at work. <P>Loyde||||reg||14
Z||000008||Phil||10-26-2001||10:54 AM||||The Fiero Store uppers have MOOG 6531 stamped on them- $12 at local parts stores- check to be sure though before removing the old ones||||reg||1
Z||000009||montage||10-26-2001||12:05 PM||||The lowers can be found at any auto parts store that sells Moog. In my area (prices are a bit high) they are around $70. At Auto Value, their house brand are made by Moog (ask the any store for the source and they will tell you) and sell for $35 each so thats what I went with. In my reseach the Fiero Store was the only source of uppers. I understood that they bought out GM's remaining stock.||||reg||1
Z||000010||mrfiero||10-26-2001||12:16 PM||||The Moog lower balljoint is part #K5297 and is listed at $61.09 at <A HREF="http://www.carparts.com." TARGET=_blank>http://www.carparts.com.</A> <P>I'm not sure where I got mine, but I don't think it was mail order.<P>The uppers I used were original GM replacements (now discontinued).  I saw the Moog uppers on someones car and was intrigued.....I think they are from another car, but I'm not sure.  I don't think Moog made any specifically for the '88 Fiero, but I could be wrong.<P>   ||||reg||1
Z||000011||summerjim||10-26-2001||01:14 PM||||The 88 uppers that the Fiero Store sells are from another GM vehicle.<P>OEM 88 uppers are all gone now. Fiero Store says that their 88 upper replacement ones "will be around for a long time to come". I believe the taper on the ball joint shaft is slightly different, but seems to work.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Wannabe||10-26-2001||02:35 PM||||Didn't somebody recently post about a fairly new ball joint failing? Was that for an '88 or earlier car? Whatever the case, there's ne doubt we need to find a good long term alternative for the '88 uppers. To make matters worse, they seem to wear quickly under hard use.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Phil||10-26-2001||03:33 PM||||The number on the Fiero Store Moog uppers go to a Caviler(sp)||||reg||1
Z||000014||artherd||10-26-2001||03:58 PM||||Hi Loyde, thanks! I'll try NAPA here locally (no 'advance, etc stores here)  If they don't stock them, I'll gladly take those off your hands  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Thanks to all who replied, this fourm rocks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>(yeah, the uppers are the really hard to find ones, and the fourm member who recently failed a *lower* (not upper) balljoint was sourced from the FieroStore. Might not mean anything (a fluke craked one?) or might indicate a potential quality problem?  I dunno, but I'll check extra hard for crakcs, even moreso than usual.   The lowers after all are the loadbearing joints  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FastFieros:<BR><B>If you can find them for $50 a piece you better buy them all. I just purchased 4 on special order from NAPA and they hit me for $92 a piece. <P>The uppers are $75 a piece also, so if you can find these please share the info.<P>I have used only 2 this last weekend so if you want to spring for the $200 for the other pair includes Postal EXPRESS mail service to your door, I will sell them to you. I can do pics or parts numbers tonight if you want to try to chase down some in CA.<P>Loyde <A HREF="http://www.fastfieros.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fastfieros.com</A> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
