Z||000016||FastFieros||10-26-2001||08:50 PM||||Here are the part numbers for the following balljoints I have purchased:<P>FA1467   McQuay-Norris  $75 (I used these)<P>260-1319  NAPA Chassis  $89 (I was close)<P>Loyde||||reg||14
Z||000017||artherd||10-27-2001||03:09 AM||||Went to local NAPA, they had 'em! ($69ea)  poped the old ones out, and pushed new ones in with a rented press (Hertz, finally, no auto parts store had such a beast) took maybe 20mintuies.<P>Thanks for all the tips, and part numbers!<P>Now I begin my search for replacement uppers (as they're 'good' now, but I want to replace everything at the same time anyway.  )<P>PS: It could well be the Caviler lower unit that is analogous to our 88 uppers... (neither one are weight-bearing)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
